# The token's "+1/+1 for each other Rat you control" counts only Rats under its controller's control (CR 613.4c). Bot2 casts Song of
# Totentanz with X = 2 (two Rat tokens) and Bot1 bolts only one: X = 1, so one Rat token is created for Bot1. Bot2 still controls a Rat,
# which must not count: the token is 2/2 (itself 1/1, +1/+1 for Vren, the one other Rat Bot1 controls), not 3/3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Vren, the Relentless
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Song of Totentanz
Forest x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Vren, the Relentless.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot2.Hand.Song of Totentanz.Cast(X: 2)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Rat Token#1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 1
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Rat Token.Power = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Rat Token.Toughness = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
